367 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 194 0 R
/E (The IPL Win Probability Prediction System covers the complete development of a machine learning-based prediction system using historical IPL datasets from 2008 to 2024. The system includes data collection, preprocessing, feature extraction, model training, and frontend development. Users can input match details such as teams, score, overs, and wickets to receive real-time probability predictions. The project ensures accurate data handling, efficient model performance, and a user-friendly interface. It can be further extended to include live match data integration, advanced visualization, and support for other sports or cricket formats. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
368 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 194 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
369 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 194 0 R
/E (The main purpose of the IPL Win Probability Prediction System is to provide a reliable and efficient platform that can predict the probability of a team winning during an ongoing IPL match. It aims to transform raw match data into meaningful insights by using machine learning techniques, allowing users to better understand match situations in real time. The system simplifies the process of prediction by analyzing important parameters such as score, overs, wickets, and target, and presenting the results in an easy-to-understand percentage format. Overall, the project focuses on enhancing user experience, improving decision-making, and demonstrating the practical application of data analytics in sports. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
