375 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E (With the growing popularity of cricket and the increasing availability of match data, users expect more advanced insights beyond traditional scoreboards. Conventional systems only display basic information such as runs and wickets, which do not fully capture the dynamic nature of the game. Therefore, there is a need for a system that can analyze real-time match conditions and provide meaningful predictions. The IPL Win Probability Prediction System fulfills this requirement by offering probability-based insights, making the match more engaging and informative for users. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
376 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E (With the increasing use of machine learning in prediction systems, the accuracy and reliability of the model have become critical factors. The system processes large volumes of IPL data, and any inconsistency or error in the dataset can affect the prediction results. Therefore, proper data preprocessing, cleaning, and feature engineering are essential to ensure high-quality input for the model. Additionally, the use of an efficient algorithm like LightGBM improves prediction accuracy and reduces computation time, ensuring that the system delivers fast and reliable results.. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
377 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E (User interaction plays a vital role in the success of any application. Many analytical systems are complex and difficult for users to understand. The IPL Win Probability Prediction System addresses this challenge by providing a simple and interactive interface using Streamlit. Users can easily input match details and receive predictions instantly without requiring technical knowledge. This improves accessibility and ensures that the system can be used by a wide range of users, including cricket fans and analysts. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
