/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 205 0 R
/E (The IPL Win Probability Prediction System follows a structured and modular architecture that integrates data processing, machine learning, and user interaction components to provide real-time predictions. The system begins with the data layer, where historical IPL datasets, including match data and ball-by-ball delivery data from 2008 to 2024, are collected and stored. This data is then passed to the preprocessing module, where it undergoes cleaning, transformation, and feature engineering to extract important parameters such as runs left, balls left, wickets remaining, current run rate \(CRR\), and required run rate \(RRR\).)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
472 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 205 0 R
/E (The processed data is used to train the machine learning model using the LightGBM algorithm in the Anaconda Jupyter Notebook environment. The trained model is then saved and integrated into the application for real-time prediction. When a user interacts with the system through the frontend interface developed using Streamlit, the input data is sent to the backend, where the trained model processes the inputs and generates the winning probability for both teams. The output is then displayed to the user in percentage format through the interface.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
