/P 206 0 R
/E (The IPL Win Probability Prediction System is based on a structured process that involves data collection, preprocessing, model training, and real-time prediction using a machine learning algorithm. The system primarily uses the Light Gradient Boosting Machine \(LightGBM\) algorithm, which is known for its high accuracy and fast performance in handling large datasets. Initially, historical IPL datasets, including match data and ball-by-ball delivery data, are collected from reliable sources such as Kaggle. This data is then preprocessed to remove inconsistencies, handle missing values, and convert it into a structured format suitable for analysis.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
478 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 206 0 R
/E (During the preprocessing stage, important features such as runs left, balls left, wickets remaining, current run rate \(CRR\), and required run rate \(RRR\) are extracted from the raw data. These features play a crucial role in determining the outcome of the match and are used as input variables for the model. The cleaned and processed data is then used to train the LightGBM model in the Anaconda Jupyter Notebook environment. The model learns patterns and relationships between input features and match outcomes, enabling it to make accurate predictions.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
