534 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 215 0 R
/E (From the user perspective, the system provides a simple and interactive interface using Streamlit, allowing users to easily input match details and obtain instant predictions. The design focuses on ease of use, ensuring that both technical and non-technical users can understand and utilize the system without difficulty. The clear presentation of results in percentage form enhances user understanding of match situations and improves overall engagement. )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
535 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 215 0 R
/E (The IPL Win Probability Prediction System successfully achieves its goal of developing a machine learning-based application for predicting match outcomes in real time. The system uses historical IPL data along with important match parameters such as score, overs, wickets, and target to generate accurate win probability predictions. The implementation of the LightGBM algorithm ensures efficient performance and reliable results, making the system effective for practical use. )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
536 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 215 0 R
/E (Overall, the project demonstrates the successful integration of machine learning, data analysis, and frontend development into a single application. It highlights the practical application of data science in sports analytics and provides valuable insights into match dynamics. The system serves as a reliable and efficient tool for prediction and also offers scope for future improvements such as live data integration and advanced analytics features. )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
